{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDE2LzM3JTIwJTI4MjAxNiUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"37","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/im8VaD4tu7lChxF9tUOG1H9sFzp.jpg","description":"On a March night in 1964, 37 neighbors in Queens, New York, witness the brutal murder of Kitty Genovese. None of them takes action or calls the police. 37 tells the story of a few of these people and what led up to the night when they unexplainably remained passive observers. The film is a convincing portrayal of a borough in change and a time characterized by racism, the Civil Rights Movement and political shifts. The actual event that inspired the film’s plot has been called a symbol for the moment when America lost its innocence. The director Puk Grasten skillfully weaves into her feature film debut various fates, dreams and family conflicts by leading us through an apartment building that comes to bear a collective failure.\n\nRated NR · Released 7 Oct 2016 · Denmark, United States of America · Language: English · 85 min\nStudio: Regner Grasten Film, Game 7 Films\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2016","genres":["Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"4.8","runtime":"85 min","cast":["Christina Brucato","Michael Potts","Maria Dizzia","Jamie Harrold","Thomas Kopache","Adrian Martinez","Samira Wiley","Lucy Martin"],"director":["Puk Grasten"],"released":"2016-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"This Poster will Be Seen But Not Heard. This Film Will Be Seen and Heard.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Puk Grasten","character":"Director"},{"name":"Christina Brucato","character":"Kitty Genovese","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/5yNLxKg9o3791d72j8XhalawFyE.jpg"},{"name":"Michael Potts","character":"Archibald Smith","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/3fgLuZkPH6F4RDjWeWt1s9bjy3v.jpg"},{"name":"Maria Dizzia","character":"Mary Cunningham","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/sMsBH9o1kuFeVgjX2QoXvxccKJQ.jpg"},{"name":"Jamie Harr